.TH LEGHORN 1 "August 2026" "leghorn 0.4.14" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
leghorn \- live dashboard for Claude Code sessions, git state, and GitHub CI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B leghorn
[\fB\-i\fR \fISECS\fR]
[\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIPACE\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-git\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-commits\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-github\fR]
[\fB\-\-github\-interval\fR \fISECS\fR]
[\fB\-\-commits\-width\fR \fICOLS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leghorn
is a full-screen curses view you leave open on a second monitor while many
Claude Code sessions work. Three panes: every live session joined to its
worktree and real git state (SESSIONS), CI runs and open PRs across every
GitHub clone with failures pinned until they go green (GITHUB), and a commit
feed across every repo and branch, newest first (COMMITS).
.PP
Read-only by construction: it reads the JSONL session transcripts written by
Claude Code, runs
.BR gh
and read-only git plumbing, and never writes to a tree, a registry or a
session. Every data source is optional and degrades to a labelled gap rather
than an error \- a session with no transcript yet shows no status or context,
and no gh authentication means the GitHub pane says it cannot see instead of
pretending nothing is happening.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECS\fR
Seconds between session/git refreshes. Overrides \fB\-\-speed\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-speed " " \fIPACE\fR
Refresh pace, one of \fBultra\fR (1s sessions / 60s gh), \fBfast\fR (5s / 75s,
the default), \fBnormal\fR (8s / 2m) or \fBslow\fR (5m / 6h). Cycle it at
runtime with \fBp\fR. The gh floor stays at a minute even on ultra: a sweep
costs seconds of network across the fleet against a rate-limited API, so a
shorter period buys overlapping sweeps rather than fresher data.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Skip the per-tree git probes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-commits
Hide the commit pane; SESSIONS and GITHUB then sit side by side as two
columns. Toggle at runtime with \fBc\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-github
Hide the GitHub pane; no gh calls are made at all.
.TP
.BR \-\-github\-interval " " \fISECS\fR
Seconds between gh sweeps. Overrides \fB\-\-speed\fR. The session loop never
waits on it.
.TP
.BR \-\-commits\-width " " \fICOLS\fR
Fix the commit pane width instead of scaling it.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B q / esc
quit
.TP
.B r
refresh everything now, including the gh sweep
.TP
.B s / f
cycle sort / filter
.TP
.B p
cycle refresh speed: ultra, fast, normal, slow
.TP
.B c
toggle the commit feed; off puts sessions and github side by side
.TP
.B g
toggle the per-tree git probes
.TP
.B tab
cycle focus: sessions, github, commits
.TP
.B j / k, arrows
move selection; 0 / G jump to top / bottom
.TP
.B enter
detail overlay for the selected row
.TP
.B ?
help: what each screen and symbol means
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEGHORN_ROOT
Directory the clones live under (default ~/GitHub). The commit feed walks
every repo in it; the GitHub pane asks gh about the ones with a github.com
origin.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gh (1),
.BR git (1)
